course: dictionary
lesson: 12014
title: Cherished: loved and kept close
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cherished is an adjective, so it describes a noun. A cherished toy is a toy that is loved very much and looked after with care. Cherish is the verb, and cherished is its past form, as in «They cherished every moment of the holiday.»
explain: Look at the words around cherished to find its meaning. «Mia kept her grandad's old watch in a box, because it was a cherished possession.» Keeping it carefully in a box tells you that Mia loves it and that it matters to her. So cherished means loved, protected and cared for very much.
explain: The word also works for memories and hopes. «Grandma spoke of her cherished memories of seaside summers.» A memory cannot be locked in a box, but Grandma keeps it safe in her heart, so cherished here means kept carefully in the mind. Always check: does your meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Cherished means loved, protected and cared for very much, as in «a cherished toy».
fact: Cherished can also mean kept carefully in your mind and heart, as in «a cherished memory» or «a cherished hope».
fact: Cherished is the past form of the verb cherish: cherish, cherishes, cherished, cherishing.
fact: Stories often use cherished to show how much a character loves a person, a pet or an old object.
fact: Families often speak of «cherished memories» of someone who has died, to show that those memories matter deeply.
exercise: «Sam carried his old teddy bear everywhere, because it was his cherished toy.» What does cherished mean here? | Broken and thrown away | Very new and shiny | Lost in the park | *Loved and cared for very much
exercise: «They cherished every moment of the holiday.» Find and copy the past form of the verb cherish. | *cherished | every | holiday | moment
exercise: «Grandma spoke of her cherished memories of seaside summers.» What does cherished suggest about the memories? | *They are kept carefully in her heart | They were written in a newspaper | They were forgotten long ago | They were all about the rain
test: «Ella kept the letter from her best friend in a box. It was a cherished letter.» What does cherished mean? | *Loved and kept with care | Torn up and thrown away | Boring and dull | Loud and noisy
test: Dad said, «I have a cherished hope that we will visit the sea again.» What kind of hope is it? | A hope about the weather tomorrow | A hope that someone else wrote down | A hope he forgot long ago | *A hope he keeps close and treasures
exam: Which phrase shows a memory that is kept carefully in the heart? | a loud noise | a quick run | *a cherished memory | a broken window
